\subsection{Datasets and RU-rationalities}

The dataset in this paper is a stochastic choice function $\hat{\rho}$ on aggregated alternatives. That is, for any $(D,x)$ such that $a \in A \subseteq \A$,  $\hat{\rho}(A,a) \ge 0$ and $\sum_{a \in A}\hat{\rho}(A,a) =1$.  Note that the stochastic choice function is defined with the set of  ${\mathscr A}$, not with the underlying alternatives $\tilde{X} \cup X^*$. Thus, we sometimes call $\hat{\rho}$ {\it reduced} dataset. For simplicity, we assume that $\hat{\rho}$ is defined on all subsets of $\A$. However this assumption is not necessary for our results.  After we present our theorems, we provide a remark in which we specify the assumption we need for the results.  (See Remark \ref{remm:dom})





