\vspace{1cm}
\begin{abstract}

We study the growth of the resolvent of a Hardy--Toeplitz operator $T_b$ with a Laurent polynomial symbol (\emph{i.e., } 
the matrix $T_b$ is banded), at the neighborhood of a point $w_0\in\pt(\s(T_b))$ on the boundary of its spectrum. We show that 
such growth is inverse linear in some non-tangential domains at the vertex $w_0$, provided that $w_0$ does not belong to a 
certain finite set on the complex plane. 
\end{abstract}




\keywords{Toeplitz operator, Hardy space, resolvent growth, Laurent polynomials, non-tangential domains.}
