In HAD receivers, the analog combiner represents a spatial sector within which the DoAs can be estimated. Received signals with DoAs 
outside this sector will be attenuated, or even nullified.
To avoid this limitation, we follow the scheme advocated in~\cite{Mona2023doa}. In this scheme, an exhaustive set of analog combiners
