\subsection{LHS\,1478\,b}

For LHS\,1478\,b visit 2 we are unable to detect an eclipse, much like in the original Hot Rocks survey paper \citep{august_hot_2024}. This supports the conclusion from \cite{august_hot_2024} that the ``sinusoidal systematic" they observe during the predicted eclipse time is likely astrophysical in origin, as our FN-PCA detrending is (by design) unable to detect astrophysical signals and does not show signs of sinusoidal variation.

